From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SystoleOS <systole@example.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] COMP: Add missing <iostream> includes for VTK 9.6

VTK 9.6 headers no longer include <iostream> transitively, nor provide
the global using-declarations for cout/cerr/clog, so code written
against older VTK fails with "'cerr' is not a member of 'std'" or
"'cerr' was not declared in this scope".  Include <iostream> in every
source file that uses these streams and qualify bare uses with std::.
---
 DiagnosticTools/DiagDataCollection.cxx                         | 1 +
 PlusServerLauncher/Testing/PlusServerLauncherRemoteControl.cxx | 1 +
 PointSetExtractor/PointSetExtractor.cxx                        | 1 +
 fCal/vtkPlusVisualizationController.cxx                        | 1 +
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/DiagnosticTools/DiagDataCollection.cxx b/DiagnosticTools/DiagDataCollection.cxx
index eb0b5cc..428a56e 100644
--- a/DiagnosticTools/DiagDataCollection.cxx
+++ b/DiagnosticTools/DiagDataCollection.cxx
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <iostream>
 /*=Plus=header=begin======================================================
